{#- Every figure is `'<id>' | num` (or `| pct`); the prose carries no numeral. -#}
{%- macro cp(a, component) -%}{{ ('cp/' ~ month ~ '/' ~ a.account_id ~ '/' ~ component) | num }}{%- endmacro -%}
{%- macro cp_pct(a, component) -%}{{ ('cp/' ~ month ~ '/' ~ a.account_id ~ '/' ~ component) | pct }}{%- endmacro -%}
{%- macro rollup(metric) -%}{{ ('rollup/' ~ month ~ '/' ~ metric) | num }}{%- endmacro -%}
{%- macro rollup_pct(metric) -%}{{ ('rollup/' ~ month ~ '/' ~ metric) | pct }}{%- endmacro -%}
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>Acme AI contribution memo, {{ month }}</title>
<style>
  body { font: 16px/1.5 system-ui, sans-serif; max-width: 60rem; margin: 2rem auto; padding: 0 1rem; color: #1b1b1b; background: #fff; }
  table { border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; }
  th, td { text-align: left; padding: .25rem .5rem; border-bottom: 1px solid #ccc; }
  td.n, th.n { text-align: right; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
  .scroll { overflow-x: auto; }
  a { color: #0b4f9c; }
  @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) { body { color: #eee; background: #111; } th, td { border-color: #444; } a { color: #8ab4f8; } }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<h1>Acme AI contribution memo, {{ month }}</h1>

<section id="page-one">
<h2>What this memo measures</h2>
<p>Contribution profit is revenue, net of credits and discounts, less inference cost, cloud cost
(direct plus allocated shared) and support cost. Support is part of cost of revenue: a customer who
leans hard on the support desk costs more to serve, and leaving that cost out would hide the accounts
that cost most. This is the project's own definition, not any company's.</p>

<h3>Headline</h3>
<p>Total revenue for {{ month }}: <strong>{{ rollup('revenue') }}</strong>.
Total contribution profit: <strong>{{ rollup('contribution_profit') }}</strong>.
Accounts flagged firm: <strong>{{ rollup('accounts_firm') }}</strong>; flagged soft:
<strong>{{ rollup('accounts_soft') }}</strong>, out of <strong>{{ rollup('accounts_active') }}</strong>
active accounts.</p>

<h3>The books are synthetic</h3>
<p>All figures are synthetic. The books belong to a generated company, Acme AI, and describe no real
customer.</p>

<h3>The seller's view of AI cost</h3>
<p>Most talk about the cost of AI is written from the buyer's side: what a call to a model costs. This
memo takes the seller's side. For a company that sells an AI product, the question is what each customer
costs to serve, in inference, cloud and support, set against what that customer pays, month after month.</p>
</section>

<section id="by-account">
<h2>Contribution profit by account</h2>
<h3>Distribution</h3>
<p>{{ rollup('accounts_active') }} accounts were active in {{ month }}, and
{{ rollup('accounts_zero_revenue') }} of them had no revenue. Among accounts with usage and positive revenue,
the lower quartile of margin is {{ rollup_pct('margin_pct_p25') }}, the median is
{{ rollup_pct('margin_pct_p50') }} and the upper quartile is {{ rollup_pct('margin_pct_p75') }}. The
lower quartile of monthly revenue is {{ rollup('revenue_p25') }} and the median is {{ rollup('revenue_p50') }}.</p>

{% for title, rows in (('Highest contribution profit', top), ('Lowest contribution profit', bottom)) %}
{% if rows %}
<h3>{{ title }}</h3>
<div class="scroll"><table>
<thead><tr><th>Account</th><th>Name</th><th class="n">Revenue</th><th class="n">Contribution profit</th>
<th class="n">Margin</th><th class="n">Trailing three-month margin</th><th>Flag</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
{% for a in rows %}
<tr data-account="{{ a.account_id }}"><td>{{ a.account_id }}</td><td>{{ a.display_name }}</td>
<td class="n">{{ cp(a, 'revenue') }}</td><td class="n">{{ cp(a, 'contribution_profit') }}</td>
<td class="n">{{ cp_pct(a, 'margin_pct') }}</td><td class="n">{{ cp_pct(a, 'trailing3_margin') }}</td>
<td>{{ ('flag/' ~ month ~ '/' ~ a.account_id) | num }}</td></tr>
{% endfor %}
</tbody>
</table></div>
{% endif %}
{% endfor %}
</section>

<section id="flagged">
<h2>Flagged accounts</h2>
<p>An account is flagged when its contribution profit is below the margin floor. It is <em>firm</em> when it
is below the floor under every allowed allocation rule and <em>soft</em> when it is below under some rules and
not others. Each flagged account carries one reason code, the cost driver furthest above its cohort's median.</p>
{% for title, rows, anchor in (('Firm', firm, 'firm-flags'), ('Soft', soft, 'soft-flags')) %}
<h3>{{ title }}</h3>
{% if rows %}
<div class="scroll"><table id="{{ anchor }}">
<thead><tr><th>Account</th><th>Name</th><th>Flag and reason</th><th class="n">Revenue</th>
<th class="n">Contribution profit</th><th class="n">Margin</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
{% for a in rows %}
<tr data-account="{{ a.account_id }}"><td>{{ a.account_id }}</td><td>{{ a.display_name }}</td>
<td>{{ ('flag/' ~ month ~ '/' ~ a.account_id) | num }}</td>
<td class="n">{{ cp(a, 'revenue') }}</td><td class="n">{{ cp(a, 'contribution_profit') }}</td>
<td class="n">{{ cp_pct(a, 'margin_pct') }}</td></tr>
{% endfor %}
</tbody>
</table></div>
{% else %}
<p>No account is flagged {{ title | lower }} this month.</p>
{% endif %}
{% endfor %}

<h3>Cost with no revenue</h3>
<p>An account with cost and no revenue has no margin to state, so its margin reads n/a. It is flagged firm by the
same arithmetic as any other account.</p>
{% if zero_revenue %}
<div class="scroll"><table id="zero-revenue">
<thead><tr><th>Account</th><th>Name</th><th class="n">Inference</th><th class="n">Cloud direct</th>
<th class="n">Cloud shared</th><th class="n">Support</th><th class="n">Contribution profit</th>
<th class="n">Margin</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
{% for a in zero_revenue %}
<tr data-account="{{ a.account_id }}"><td>{{ a.account_id }}</td><td>{{ a.display_name }}</td>
<td class="n">{{ cp(a, 'inference_cost') }}</td><td class="n">{{ cp(a, 'cloud_direct') }}</td>
<td class="n">{{ cp(a, 'cloud_shared') }}</td><td class="n">{{ cp(a, 'support_cost') }}</td>
<td class="n">{{ cp(a, 'contribution_profit') }}</td><td class="n">{{ cp_pct(a, 'margin_pct') }}</td></tr>
{% endfor %}
</tbody>
</table></div>
{% else %}
<p>No active account has cost without revenue this month.</p>
{% endif %}
</section>

<section id="allocation">
<h2>Allocation rule</h2>
<p>Shared cloud cost has no owner, so it is spread over accounts by a rule. The recommended rule is
<code>{{ recommended }}</code>. Contribution profit by account, and so the flags, depend on that choice; the
tables below show how much.</p>
{% if changes %}
<h3>Accounts whose status changes</h3>
<table id="status-changes">
<thead><tr><th>Rule</th><th class="n">Accounts changing status against the recommended rule</th><th>Accounts</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
{% for c in changes %}
<tr data-rule="{{ c.rule }}"><td><code>{{ c.rule }}</code></td>
<td class="n">{{ ('rollup/' ~ month ~ '/accounts_status_change_' ~ c.rule) | num }}</td>
<td>{{ c.accounts | join(', ') }}</td></tr>
{% endfor %}
</tbody>
</table>
{% endif %}

{% if spread %}
<h3>Spread across rules</h3>
<p>Contribution profit of each flagged account under each allowed rule.</p>
<div class="scroll"><table id="rule-spread">
<thead><tr><th>Account</th>{% for rule in rules %}<th class="n"><code>{{ rule }}</code></th>{% endfor %}</tr></thead>
<tbody>
{% for a in spread %}
<tr data-account="{{ a.account_id }}"><td>{{ a.account_id }}</td>
{% for rule in rules %}<td class="n">{{ ('cpr/' ~ month ~ '/' ~ a.account_id ~ '/' ~ rule) | num }}</td>{% endfor %}</tr>
{% endfor %}
</tbody>
</table></div>
{% endif %}

<h3>Why <code>{{ recommended }}</code></h3>
<p>The synthetic books were generated with shared cloud cost that scales with inference volume, measured in
tokens, and <code>{{ recommended }}</code> allocates it the same way. The recommendation is consistent with how
the data was constructed. It is not evidence about how the shared cloud cost of any real business behaves.</p>
</section>

<section id="actions">
<h2>Actions</h2>
<p>Each firm-flagged account gets the action its reason code dictates, by a fixed rule:</p>
<ul>
<li><code>DEEP_DISCOUNT</code> or <code>DEDICATED_CLOUD</code>: reprice at renewal.</li>
<li><code>MODEL_MIX</code>: migrate to a plan priced per model.</li>
<li><code>SUPPORT_LOAD</code> with revenue below the lower quartile of revenue, {{ rollup('revenue_p25') }}: let the
account churn. With revenue at or above it: reprice.</li>
</ul>
{% if actions %}
<div class="scroll"><table id="action-table">
<thead><tr><th>Account</th><th>Name</th><th>Reason</th><th class="n">Revenue</th><th>Action</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
{% for a in actions %}
<tr data-account="{{ a.account_id }}" data-action="{{ a.action }}"><td>{{ a.account_id }}</td><td>{{ a.display_name }}</td>
<td><code>{{ a.reason_code }}</code></td><td class="n">{{ cp(a, 'revenue') }}</td><td>{{ a.action_text }}</td></tr>
{% endfor %}
</tbody>
</table></div>
{% else %}
<p>No account is flagged firm this month, so there is no action to take.</p>
{% endif %}
</section>

<section id="scenario">
<h2>Token-price scenario</h2>
{% if scenario %}
<p>This section asks what would happen to the flagged accounts if the price of model inference kept falling
at the pace it has fallen. It applies a real published trend to the synthetic accounts of {{ month }}: an
illustrative what-if relative to {{ month }}, not a forecast made then.</p>

<h3>The trend</h3>
<p>The series is the blended list price per million tokens of three model tiers, each tier at the newest
generally available model of one vendor's line, read from the vendor's own price page. Input tokens count
three times and output tokens once, and the tiers count equally. Every price below is cited to the row it was
read from, with the page it came from and the date it was retrieved.</p>
<div class="scroll"><table id="price-trend">
<thead><tr><th>Tier</th><th class="n">Price in {{ scenario.first }}</th><th>Source</th>
<th class="n">Price in {{ scenario.last }}</th><th>Source</th><th>Retrieved</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
{% for t in scenario.trend %}
<tr data-tier="{{ t.tier }}"><td>{{ t.tier }}</td>
<td class="n">{{ t.first.price | cite(t.ref) }}</td><td><a href="{{ t.first.source_url }}">price page</a></td>
<td class="n">{{ t.last.price | cite(t.ref) }}</td><td><a href="{{ t.last.source_url }}">price page</a></td>
<td>{{ t.last.retrieved_on | cite(t.ref) }}</td></tr>
{% endfor %}
</tbody>
</table></div>

<h3>Method</h3>
<p>The blended price changed by <strong>{{ ('scenario/' ~ month ~ '/summary/computed_change') | num }}</strong>
between {{ scenario.first }} and {{ scenario.last }}, a compound monthly rate of
<strong>{{ ('scenario/' ~ month ~ '/summary/monthly_rate') | num }}</strong> over the six months. The
scenario applies that rate to each flagged account's inference cost month by month, holding volume,
revenue, support, cloud cost and Acme's own prices at their {{ month }} values. It runs the rate at full
persistence, at half of it and at none. An account below the floor under the signed rule recovers in the first
quarter, counted from the month after {{ month }}, whose last month puts it above the floor.</p>

<h3>Output</h3>
<p>The scenario covers the <strong>{{ rollup('accounts_firm') }}</strong> accounts flagged firm and, listed
separately below each firm table, the <strong>{{ rollup('accounts_soft') }}</strong> flagged soft. The counts
here include both kinds.</p>
<div class="scroll"><table id="scenario-recovered">
<thead><tr><th>Case</th><th class="n">Persistence</th>{% for q in scenario.quarters %}<th class="n">Recovered by {{ q }}</th>{% endfor %}</tr></thead>
<tbody>
{% for c in scenario.cases %}
<tr data-case="{{ c.case }}"><td>{{ c.case }}</td>
<td class="n">{{ ('scenario/' ~ month ~ '/' ~ c.case ~ '/summary/persistence_pct') | pct }}</td>
{% for q in scenario.quarters %}<td class="n">{{ ('scenario/' ~ month ~ '/' ~ c.case ~ '/summary/accounts_recovered_' ~ q) | num }}</td>
{% endfor %}</tr>
{% endfor %}
</tbody>
</table></div>

{% for c in scenario.cases %}
<h3>Case {{ c.case }}</h3>
{% for title, kind, rows in (('Firm-flagged accounts', 'firm', c.firm), ('Soft-flagged accounts', 'soft', c.soft)) %}
<h4>{{ title }}</h4>
{% if rows %}
<div class="scroll"><table id="scenario-{{ kind }}-{{ c.case }}">
<thead><tr><th>Account</th><th>Name</th><th>Flag and reason</th><th>Recovery quarter</th>{% for q in scenario.quarters %}<th class="n">Margin at the end of {{ q }}</th>{% endfor %}</tr></thead>
<tbody>
{% for a in rows %}
<tr data-account="{{ a.account_id }}"><td>{{ a.account_id }}</td><td>{{ a.display_name }}</td>
<td>{{ ('flag/' ~ month ~ '/' ~ a.account_id) | num }}</td>
<td>{{ ('scenario/' ~ month ~ '/' ~ c.case ~ '/summary/' ~ a.account_id ~ '/recovery_quarter') | num }}</td>
{% for q in scenario.quarters %}<td class="n">{{ ('scenario/' ~ month ~ '/' ~ c.case ~ '/' ~ q ~ '/' ~ a.account_id ~ '/margin_pct') | pct }}</td>
{% endfor %}</tr>
{% endfor %}
</tbody>
</table></div>
{% else %}
<p>No account is flagged {{ kind }} this month.</p>
{% endif %}
{% endfor %}
{% endfor %}

<h3>What this does not show</h3>
<p>The series is a blend of model vendors' list prices with fixed weights. It is not Acme's per-model price
and not any customer's cost. The scenario applies a real published trend to synthetic accounts: it is an
illustrative what-if relative to {{ month }}, not a forecast made then.</p>
{% else %}
<p>The scenario has not been run for this month.</p>
{% endif %}
</section>

<section id="build-vs-buy">
<h2>Build versus buy</h2>
{% if bvb_present %}
<p>The question is whether to buy a vendor's product for this job or to keep the tool that was built. A vendor
is bought when its annual list price is below the build cost spread over twelve months, plus twelve months of
run cost, plus a maintenance allowance; otherwise the tool is kept. The allowance is an input, stated as one
tenth of the build cost per year.</p>

<h3>What the build cost</h3>
<p>Each figure is measured, not estimated, and carries the source it was collected from.</p>
<div class="scroll"><table id="build-cost">
<thead><tr><th>Measure</th><th class="n">Figure</th><th>Source</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
<tr data-measure="build_cost"><td>Model spend</td><td class="n">{{ 'bvb/build_cost' | num }}</td><td>{{ bvb_build_source | cite('ref/build_cost/build_cost_usd') }}</td></tr>
{% for m in bvb_measures %}
<tr data-measure="{{ m.ref }}"><td>{{ m.label }}</td><td class="n">{{ m.shown | cite(m.ref) }}</td><td>{{ m.source | cite(m.ref) }}</td></tr>
{% endfor %}
<tr data-measure="run_cost_monthly"><td>Run cost for a month</td><td class="n">{{ bvb_run_monthly | cite(bvb_run_ref) }}</td><td>{{ bvb_run_source | cite(bvb_run_ref) }}</td></tr>
</tbody>
</table></div>

<h3>The cost to beat</h3>
<div class="scroll"><table id="cost-to-beat">
<thead><tr><th>Part of the yearly cost of keeping the tool</th><th class="n">Amount</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
<tr><td>Build cost spread over the year</td><td class="n">{{ 'bvb/build_cost_amortised' | num }}</td></tr>
<tr><td>Run cost for the year</td><td class="n">{{ 'bvb/run_cost_annual' | num }}</td></tr>
<tr><td>Maintenance allowance</td><td class="n">{{ 'bvb/maintenance_allowance' | num }}</td></tr>
</tbody>
</table></div>

<h3>Vendors selling the same job</h3>
{% if bvb_vendors %}
<p>Each price is the vendor's published list price for a year, cited to the page it was read from and the date
it was retrieved.</p>
<div class="scroll"><table id="vendor-verdicts">
<thead><tr><th>Vendor</th><th class="n">Annual list price</th><th>Verdict</th><th>Source</th><th>Retrieved</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
{% for v in bvb_vendors %}
<tr data-vendor="{{ v.vendor }}" data-verdict="{{ v.verdict }}"><td>{{ v.product }}</td><td class="n">{{ v.id | num }}</td>
<td>{{ v.verdict }}</td><td><a href="{{ v.source_url }}">price page</a></td>
<td>{{ v.retrieved_on | cite(v.ref) }}</td></tr>
{% endfor %}
</tbody>
</table></div>
{% else %}
<p>No vendor list prices have been collected yet.</p>
{% endif %}
{% else %}
<p>The build cost has not been collected yet, so this section has no figures.</p>
{% endif %}
</section>

<section id="controls">
<h2>Controls and limits</h2>
<h3>Controls</h3>
<p>The month closed only after every control below ran on it:</p>
<ul id="control-list">
{% for control in controls %}<li>{{ control }}</li>
{% endfor %}</ul>

<h3>Tie-out to the general ledger</h3>
<p>Account revenue less the ledger, by revenue code. Every difference must be zero for the month to close.</p>
<table>
<thead><tr><th>GL code</th><th class="n">Difference</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
{% for code in gl_codes %}
<tr><td>{{ code }}</td><td class="n">{{ ('pnl/' ~ month ~ '/' ~ code) | num }}</td></tr>
{% endfor %}
</tbody>
</table>

<h3>Agreement between interfaces</h3>
<p>A number can be asked for through the command line, through SQL, through this page and through the cached
values file. Whether the four agree for every account is checked after this page is built, and the result is
published beside it as <a href="agreement.json" data-deferred="agreement">agreement.json</a>. This page does
not embed that result, because a page cannot contain the outcome of a check over itself.</p>

<h3>Planted errors</h3>
<p>Each error the injection command knows is planted in a copy of the example books and closed. The control
that names it and the steps that fix the books are shown in the <a href="../errors/index.html">planted-errors
gallery</a>.</p>

<h3>Limits</h3>
<ul>
<li>Sign-off: a public demo cannot enforce separation of duties. Whoever can run the commands can also approve
the configuration, and the <code>producer_kind</code> on each provenance record, <code>workflow</code> or
<code>agent</code>, is declared by the process that writes it, not verified.</li>
<li>The injected-error tests copy the books, plant a known error and require the matching control to fail and
name the rows. They prove those controls catch those errors. They do not prove that no other error exists.</li>
<li>This first version uses synthetic books only, writes its prose from fixed templates with no model-written
commentary, does not forecast, and allocates shared cloud cost by one of the stated rules rather than measuring
it per customer.</li>
</ul>
</section>

<section id="appendix">
<h2>Appendix</h2>
<h3>Method</h3>
<p>Each account's revenue is its invoiced platform fees and usage less credits. Inference cost prices each
account's tokens by model. Direct cloud cost is cost tagged to the account; shared cloud cost is spread by the
allocation rule. Support cost is handled minutes at the rate for the ticket's tier. Contribution profit is
revenue less those four costs, in whole cents. Margin is contribution profit as a share of revenue, rounded
half-even to four decimal places, and n/a where revenue is zero.</p>
<p>Every figure on this page carries its number ID. <code>margin explain &lt;number-id&gt;</code> prints the
chain from the figure down to the hashed source rows. The code is in the
<a href="{{ repository }}">project repository</a>.</p>

<h3>Definitions</h3>
<dl>
<dt>Active account</dt><dd>An account with any invoice, usage, tagged-cost or ticket row in the month.</dd>
<dt>Firm flag</dt><dd>Contribution profit below the floor under every allowed allocation rule.</dd>
<dt>Soft flag</dt><dd>Contribution profit below the floor under some allowed rules but not all.</dd>
<dt>Quartile</dt><dd>The value at the nearest rank in the sorted values, taken over accounts with usage and positive revenue.</dd>
</dl>

<h3>Every checked figure</h3>
<p>The table holds each account's six cents components and margin, then the six month totals. Each cell carries
its number ID and its unrounded value.</p>
<div class="scroll"><table id="appendix-table">
<thead><tr><th>Account</th><th>Name</th><th class="n">Revenue</th><th class="n">Inference</th>
<th class="n">Cloud direct</th><th class="n">Cloud shared</th><th class="n">Support</th>
<th class="n">Contribution profit</th><th class="n">Margin</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
{% for a in accounts %}
<tr data-account="{{ a.account_id }}"><td>{{ a.account_id }}</td><td>{{ a.display_name }}</td>
{% for c in ('revenue', 'inference_cost', 'cloud_direct', 'cloud_shared', 'support_cost', 'contribution_profit') %}<td class="n">{{ cp(a, c) }}</td>
{% endfor %}<td class="n">{{ cp_pct(a, 'margin_pct') }}</td></tr>
{% endfor %}
</tbody>
<tfoot>
<tr data-row="totals"><td>Month total</td><td></td>
{% for c in ('revenue', 'inference_cost', 'cloud_direct', 'cloud_shared', 'support_cost', 'contribution_profit') %}<td class="n">{{ rollup(c) }}</td>
{% endfor %}<td></td></tr>
</tfoot>
</table></div>
</section>
</body>
</html>
